+# Fully async MOPD adaptation
+
+This experimental campaign extends the class-based SGLang generation endpoint to request and retain student top-k candidate scores. It preserves score order across resumed responses and fails if candidate rows are missing or misaligned. Candidate loss and teacher routing retain the PR3116 implementation.
+
+The launcher accepts `--fully-async --no-colocate --use-rollout-logprobs`. The rollout GPU count is independent of `--rollout-gpus-per-engine`. Fully async execution uses `train_async.py` and the standard class-based worker. The buffer and staleness controls remain native Miles controls. Behavior-policy candidate probabilities remain the denominator rather than scores recomputed under a newer learner.
+
+Evaluation must use the same fully async rollout owner so producer pauses remain coordinated. The campaign passes an evaluation configuration with `metadata_overrides: {mopd_evaluation: true}` and a reward adapter that selects the existing puzzle verifier for those samples. Training continues to use teacher scoring. The legacy evaluation callback is not selected for this mode.
+
+The campaign keeps raw logs and compact framework metrics, but disables GPU profilers, full HTTP exchanges, and debug tensor dumps. All results must identify asynchronous sampling and the configured policy staleness bound. GPU hardware comparisons require an identical collection policy and scientific recipe.
